(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State and prove Euler's Theorem on Homogeneous Functions of degree n for two independent variables: x*\(du/dx\) + y*\(du/dy\) = n*u.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition of Homogeneous Function:) Tj
T*
(   A function u = f\(x, y\) is called homogeneous of degree n if:) Tj
T*
(   f\(t*x, t*y\) = t^n * f\(x, y\) for all t > 0.) Tj
T*
(   2. Formal Statement of Euler's Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   If u = f\(x, y\) is a homogeneous function of degree n possessing continuous first partial) Tj
T*
(   derivatives, then:) Tj
T*
(   x * \(du / dx\) + y * \(du / dy\) = n * u.) Tj
T*
(   3. Mathematical Proof:) Tj
T*
(   - Start with the defining identity:) Tj
T*
(   f\(t*x, t*y\) = t^n * f\(x, y\). \(Eq. 1\)) Tj
T*
(   - Let X = t * x and Y = t * y. The left-hand side is f\(X, Y\).) Tj
T*
(   - Differentiate both sides of Eq. 1 with respect to parameter t using the multivariable chain) Tj
T*
(   rule:) Tj
T*
(   d/dt [ f\(X, Y\) ] = d/dt [ t^n * f\(x, y\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Left-hand side:) Tj
T*
(   d/dt [ f\(X, Y\) ] = \(df / dX\) * \(dX / dt\) + \(df / dY\) * \(dY / dt\).) Tj
T*
(   Since X = t*x => dX/dt = x, and Y = t*y => dY/dt = y:) Tj
T*
(   d/dt [ f\(X, Y\) ] = \(df / dX\) * x + \(df / dY\) * y.) Tj
T*
(   - Right-hand side:) Tj
T*
(   d/dt [ t^n * f\(x, y\) ] = n * t^\(n - 1\) * f\(x, y\).) Tj
T*
(   - Equate left and right sides:) Tj
T*
(   x * \(df / dX\) + y * \(df / dY\) = n * t^\(n - 1\) * f\(x, y\). \(Eq. 2\)) Tj
T*
(   - Since Eq. 2 holds for all t > 0, set t = 1:) Tj
T*
(   When t = 1, X = 1*x = x, and Y = 1*y = y.) Tj
T*
(   df/dX becomes df/dx, df/dY becomes df/dy, and t^\(n-1\) = 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Eq. 2 simplifies to:) Tj
T*
(   x * \(df / dx\) + y * \(df / dy\) = n * f\(x, y\) = n * u.) Tj
T*
(   Hence proved.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
