(   [Problem Statement]: Prove the second-order extension of Euler's Theorem: If u\(x, y\) is homogeneous of degree n, then x^2*\(d^2u/dx^2\) + 2xy*\(d^2u/dxdy\) + y^2*\(d^2u/dy^2\) = n*\(n - 1\)*u.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Start from the first-order Euler identity:) Tj
T*
(   x * \(du / dx\) + y * \(du / dy\) = n * u. \(Eq. 1\)) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Differentiate Eq. 1 partially with respect to x:) Tj
T*
(   d/dx [ x * \(du/dx\) + y * \(du/dy\) ] = d/dx [ n * u ]) Tj
T*
(   => 1 * \(du/dx\) + x * \(d^2u / dx^2\) + y * \(d^2u / dxdy\) = n * \(du/dx\)) Tj
T*
(   => x * \(d^2u / dx^2\) + y * \(d^2u / dxdy\) = \(n - 1\) * \(du/dx\). \(Eq. 2\)) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Differentiate Eq. 1 partially with respect to y:) Tj
T*
(   d/dy [ x * \(du/dx\) + y * \(du/dy\) ] = d/dy [ n * u ]) Tj
T*
(   => x * \(d^2u / dydx\) + 1 * \(du/dy\) + y * \(d^2u / dy^2\) = n * \(du/dy\).) Tj
T*
(   By Clairaut's theorem, d^2u/dydx = d^2u/dxdy:) Tj
T*
(   => x * \(d^2u / dxdy\) + y * \(d^2u / dy^2\) = \(n - 1\) * \(du/dy\). \(Eq. 3\)) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Multiply Eq. 2 by x and Eq. 3 by y:) Tj
T*
(   x * [ x * \(d^2u / dx^2\) + y * \(d^2u / dxdy\) ] = \(n - 1\) * x * \(du/dx\)) Tj
T*
(   => x^2 * \(d^2u / dx^2\) + xy * \(d^2u / dxdy\) = \(n - 1\) * x * \(du/dx\). \(Eq. 4\)) Tj
T*
(   y * [ x * \(d^2u / dxdy\) + y * \(d^2u / dy^2\) ] = \(n - 1\) * y * \(du/dy\)) Tj
T*
(   => xy * \(d^2u / dxdy\) + y^2 * \(d^2u / dy^2\) = \(n - 1\) * y * \(du/dy\). \(Eq. 5\)) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Add Eq. 4 and Eq. 5:) Tj
T*
(   x^2 * \(d^2u / dx^2\) + 2xy * \(d^2u / dxdy\) + y^2 * \(d^2u / dy^2\) = \(n - 1\) * [ x * \(du/dx\) + y *) Tj
T*
(   \(du/dy\) ].) Tj
T*
(   Step 6: Substitute Eq. 1 into the right-hand side:) Tj
T*
(   x * \(du/dx\) + y * \(du/dy\) = n * u.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore:) Tj
T*
(   x^2 * \(d^2u / dx^2\) + 2xy * \(d^2u / dxdy\) + y^2 * \(d^2u / dy^2\) = \(n - 1\) * \(n * u\)) Tj
T*
(   = n * \(n - 1\) * u.) Tj
T*
(   Hence proved.) Tj
T*
