12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: If u = arcsin\(\(x + y\) / \(sqrt\(x\) + sqrt\(y\)\)\), prove that: \(i\) x*\(du/dx\) + y*\(du/dy\) = \(1/2\)*tan\(u\), and \(ii\) x^2*\(d^2u/dx^2\) + 2xy*\(d^2u/dxdy\) + y^2*\(d^2u/dy^2\) = -\(1/4\)*tan\(u\)*cos\(2u\) / cos^2\(u\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Set z = sin\(u\):) Tj
T*
(   z = sin\(u\) = \(x + y\) / \(sqrt\(x\) + sqrt\(y\)\) = f\(x, y\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Check homogeneity of z:) Tj
T*
(   f\(tx, ty\) = \(tx + ty\) / \(sqrt\(tx\) + sqrt\(ty\)\) = t*\(x + y\) / [ t^\(1/2\)*\(sqrt\(x\) + sqrt\(y\)\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = t^\(1 - 1/2\) * f\(x, y\) = t^\(1/2\) * f\(x, y\).) Tj
T*
(   Thus, z is a homogeneous function of degree n = 1/2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Apply Euler's Theorem to z:) Tj
T*
(   x * \(dz/dx\) + y * \(dz/dy\) = n * z = \(1/2\) * z.) Tj
T*
(   Since z = sin\(u\):) Tj
T*
(   dz/dx = cos\(u\) * \(du/dx\), dz/dy = cos\(u\) * \(du/dy\).) Tj
T*
(   Substitute:) Tj
T*
(   x * [ cos\(u\) * \(du/dx\) ] + y * [ cos\(u\) * \(du/dy\) ] = \(1/2\) * sin\(u\).) Tj
T*
(   Divide by cos\(u\):) Tj
T*
(   x * \(du/dx\) + y * \(du/dy\) = \(1/2\) * [ sin\(u\) / cos\(u\) ] = \(1/2\) * tan\(u\). \(Part i proved\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Second-Order Derivation \(Part ii\):) Tj
T*
(   Let F\(u\) = \(1/2\) * tan\(u\).) Tj
T*
(   By the Generalized Euler second-order formula for composite functions:) Tj
T*
ET

