BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: If u = arctan\(\(x^3 + y^3\) / \(x - y\)\), prove that: \(i\) x*\(du/dx\) + y*\(du/dy\) = sin\(2u\), and \(ii\) x^2*\(d^2u/dx^2\) + 2xy*\(d^2u/dxdy\) + y^2*\(d^2u/dy^2\) = 2*cos\(3u\)*sin\(u\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Set z = tan\(u\):) Tj
T*
(   z = tan\(u\) = \(x^3 + y^3\) / \(x - y\) = f\(x, y\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Check homogeneity of z:) Tj
T*
(   f\(tx, ty\) = \(t^3*x^3 + t^3*y^3\) / \(tx - ty\) = t^3*\(x^3 + y^3\) / [ t*\(x - y\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = t^2 * f\(x, y\).) Tj
T*
(   Thus, z is a homogeneous function of degree n = 2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Apply Euler's Theorem to z:) Tj
T*
(   x * \(dz/dx\) + y * \(dz/dy\) = n * z = 2 * z.) Tj
T*
(   Since z = tan\(u\):) Tj
T*
(   dz/dx = sec^2\(u\) * \(du/dx\), dz/dy = sec^2\(u\) * \(du/dy\).) Tj
T*
(   Substitute:) Tj
T*
(   x * [ sec^2\(u\) * \(du/dx\) ] + y * [ sec^2\(u\) * \(du/dy\) ] = 2 * tan\(u\)) Tj
T*
(   => sec^2\(u\) * [ x*\(du/dx\) + y*\(du/dy\) ] = 2 * tan\(u\)) Tj
T*
(   => x*\(du/dx\) + y*\(du/dy\) = 2 * tan\(u\) / sec^2\(u\)) Tj
T*
(   = 2 * [ sin\(u\) / cos\(u\) ] * cos^2\(u\)) Tj
T*
(   = 2 * sin\(u\) * cos\(u\) = sin\(2u\). \(Part i proved\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Second-Order Derivation \(Part ii\):) Tj
T*
(   Let F\(u\) = sin\(2u\).) Tj
T*
(   Using the general formula: x^2*u_xx + 2xy*u_xy + y^2*u_yy = F\(u\) * [ F'\(u\) - 1 ]:) Tj
T*
(   - F'\(u\) = d/du [ sin\(2u\) ] = 2 * cos\(2u\).) Tj
T*
(   - F\(u\) * [ F'\(u\) - 1 ] = sin\(2u\) * [ 2 * cos\(2u\) - 1 ]) Tj
T*
(   = 2 * sin\(2u\) * cos\(2u\) - sin\(2u\)) Tj
T*
(   = sin\(4u\) - sin\(2u\).) Tj
T*
(   - Use trigonometric difference formula sin A - sin B = 2 * cos\(\(A+B\)/2\) * sin\(\(A-B\)/2\):) Tj
T*
(   sin\(4u\) - sin\(2u\) = 2 * cos\(\(4u + 2u\)/2\) * sin\(\(4u - 2u\)/2\)) Tj
T*
(   = 2 * cos\(3u\) * sin\(u\).) Tj
T*
(   Hence:) Tj
T*
(   x^2*\(d^2u/dx^2\) + 2xy*\(d^2u/dxdy\) + y^2*\(d^2u/dy^2\) = 2 * cos\(3u\) * sin\(u\). \(Part ii proved\).) Tj
T*
