(   [Problem Statement]: Define the Total Differential of a function z = f\(x, y\) and derive the Chain Rule for composite functions z = f\(x, y\), where x = x\(t\) and y = y\(t\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition of Total Differential:) Tj
T*
(   - Let z = f\(x, y\) be defined on an open set D in R^2.) Tj
T*
(   - We say f is differentiable at \(x, y\) if the increment Delta_z = f\(x + Delta_x, y + Delta_y\) -) Tj
T*
(   f\(x, y\) can be written as:) Tj
T*
(   Delta_z = \(df/dx\) * Delta_x + \(df/dy\) * Delta_y + epsilon1 * Delta_x + epsilon2 * Delta_y,) Tj
T*
ET

