(   [Problem Statement]: If z = f\(u, v\) where u = x^2 - y^2 and v = 2xy, prove that: \(dz/dx\)^2 + \(dz/dy\)^2 = 4 * \(x^2 + y^2\) * [ \(dz/du\)^2 + \(dz/dv\)^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Compute partial derivatives of u and v with respect to x and y:) Tj
T*
(   u = x^2 - y^2 => du/dx = 2x, du/dy = -2y.) Tj
T*
(   v = 2xy => dv/dx = 2y, dv/dy = 2x.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Apply Chain Rule for dz/dx:) Tj
T*
(   dz/dx = \(dz/du\) * \(du/dx\) + \(dz/dv\) * \(dv/dx\)) Tj
T*
(   = \(dz/du\) * \(2x\) + \(dz/dv\) * \(2y\)) Tj
T*
(   = 2 * [ x * \(dz/du\) + y * \(dz/dv\) ].) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Square dz/dx:) Tj
T*
(   \(dz/dx\)^2 = 4 * [ x^2 * \(dz/du\)^2 + 2xy * \(dz/du\)*\(dz/dv\) + y^2 * \(dz/dv\)^2 ]. \(Eq. 1\)) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Apply Chain Rule for dz/dy:) Tj
T*
(   dz/dy = \(dz/du\) * \(du/dy\) + \(dz/dv\) * \(dv/dy\)) Tj
T*
(   = \(dz/du\) * \(-2y\) + \(dz/dv\) * \(2x\)) Tj
T*
(   = 2 * [ -y * \(dz/du\) + x * \(dz/dv\) ].) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Square dz/dy:) Tj
T*
(   \(dz/dy\)^2 = 4 * [ y^2 * \(dz/du\)^2 - 2xy * \(dz/du\)*\(dz/dv\) + x^2 * \(dz/dv\)^2 ]. \(Eq. 2\)) Tj
T*
(   Step 6: Add Eq. 1 and Eq. 2:) Tj
T*
(   \(dz/dx\)^2 + \(dz/dy\)^2 = 4 * [ \(x^2 + y^2\)*\(dz/du\)^2 + \(2xy - 2xy\)*\(dz/du\)*\(dz/dv\) + \(x^2 +) Tj
T*
(   y^2\)*\(dz/dv\)^2 ]) Tj
T*
(   = 4 * [ \(x^2 + y^2\) * \(dz/du\)^2 + 0 + \(x^2 + y^2\) * \(dz/dv\)^2 ]) Tj
T*
(   = 4 * \(x^2 + y^2\) * [ \(dz/du\)^2 + \(dz/dv\)^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   Hence proved.) Tj
T*
