(   - Let F\(x, y\) = 0 define y implicitly as a differentiable function of x.) Tj
T*
(   - Taking the total differential: dF = Fx * dx + Fy * dy = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Solving for dy/dx:) Tj
T*
(   dy / dx = - Fx / Fy \(provided Fy != 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Second derivative d^2y / dx^2:) Tj
T*
(   d^2y / dx^2 = d/dx [ - Fx / Fy ] = - [ Fy * d/dx\(Fx\) - Fx * d/dx\(Fy\) ] / \(Fy\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   By chain rule:) Tj
T*
(   d/dx\(Fx\) = Fxx + Fxy * \(dy/dx\) = Fxx - Fxy * \(Fx / Fy\) = \(Fxx * Fy - Fxy * Fx\) / Fy.) Tj
T*
(   d/dx\(Fy\) = Fyx + Fyy * \(dy/dx\) = Fyx - Fyy * \(Fx / Fy\) = \(Fxy * Fy - Fyy * Fx\) / Fy.) Tj
T*
(   Substitute into numerator:) Tj
T*
(   d^2y / dx^2 = - [ Fy * \(Fxx*Fy - Fxy*Fx\) - Fx * \(Fxy*Fy - Fyy*Fx\) ] / \(Fy\)^3) Tj
T*
(   = - [ Fxx * Fy^2 - 2 * Fxy * Fx * Fy + Fyy * Fx^2 ] / \(Fy\)^3. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Application to Folium of Descartes: F\(x, y\) = x^3 + y^3 - 3axy = 0:) Tj
T*
(   - Compute partial derivatives:) Tj
T*
(   Fx = 3x^2 - 3ay = 3*\(x^2 - ay\).) Tj
T*
(   Fy = 3y^2 - 3ax = 3*\(y^2 - ax\).) Tj
T*
(   Fxx = 6x, Fxy = -3a, Fyy = 6y.) Tj
T*
(   - First derivative dy/dx:) Tj
T*
(   dy / dx = - Fx / Fy = - [ 3*\(x^2 - ay\) ] / [ 3*\(y^2 - ax\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(ay - x^2\) / \(y^2 - ax\).) Tj
T*
(   - Second derivative d^2y/dx^2:) Tj
T*
(   Numerator N = 6x*\(3\(y^2 - ax\)\)^2 - 2*\(-3a\)*\(3\(x^2 - ay\)\)*\(3\(y^2 - ax\)\) + 6y*\(3\(x^2 - ay\)\)^2) Tj
T*
(   = 54 * [ x*\(y^2 - ax\)^2 + a*\(x^2 - ay\)*\(y^2 - ax\) + y*\(x^2 - ay\)^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   Expanding and using x^3 + y^3 = 3axy simplifies the bracket to: -2a^3*xy.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore:) Tj
T*
(   d^2y / dx^2 = - 2a^3 * x * y / \(y^2 - ax\)^3.) Tj
T*
