BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State and prove the Chain Rule for Jacobians: If u, v are functions of x, y and x, y are functions of r, theta, then d\(u, v\)/d\(r, theta\) = [d\(u, v\)/d\(x, y\)] * [d\(x, y\)/d\(r, theta\)].) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Formal Statement:) Tj
T*
(   Let u = u\(x, y\) and v = v\(x, y\) possess continuous partial derivatives with respect to x and y,) Tj
T*
(   and let x = x\(r, theta\) and y = y\(r, theta\) possess continuous partial derivatives with respect) Tj
T*
(   to r and theta. Then:) Tj
T*
(   d\(u, v\) / d\(r, theta\) = [ d\(u, v\) / d\(x, y\) ] * [ d\(x, y\) / d\(r, theta\) ].) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Proof:) Tj
T*
(   - By the multivariable chain rule:) Tj
T*
(   du/dr = \(du/dx\)*\(dx/dr\) + \(du/dy\)*\(dy/dr\)) Tj
T*
(   du/dtheta = \(du/dx\)*\(dx/dtheta\) + \(du/dy\)*\(dy/dtheta\)) Tj
T*
(   dv/dr = \(dv/dx\)*\(dx/dr\) + \(dv/dy\)*\(dy/dr\)) Tj
T*
(   dv/dtheta = \(dv/dx\)*\(dx/dtheta\) + \(dv/dy\)*\(dy/dtheta\).) Tj
T*
(   - Express these four equations simultaneously as a matrix product:) Tj
T*
(   [ du/dr, du/dtheta ] [ du/dx, du/dy ] [ dx/dr, dx/dtheta ]) Tj
T*
(   [ ] = [ ] * [ ].) Tj
T*
(   [ dv/dr, dv/dtheta ] [ dv/dx, dv/dy ] [ dy/dr, dy/dtheta ]) Tj
T*
(   - Let A = [ du/dx, du/dy; dv/dx, dv/dy ] and B = [ dx/dr, dx/dtheta; dy/dr, dy/dtheta ].) Tj
T*
(   - The matrix on the left is C = A * B.) Tj
T*
(   - Take the determinant of both sides:) Tj
T*
(   det\(C\) = det\(A * B\).) Tj
T*
(   - By the multiplicative property of determinants \(det\(A * B\) = det\(A\) * det\(B\)\):) Tj
T*
(   det\(C\) = det\(A\) * det\(B\).) Tj
T*
(   - Recognizing each determinant as a Jacobian:) Tj
T*
(   det\(C\) = d\(u, v\) / d\(r, theta\).) Tj
T*
(   det\(A\) = d\(u, v\) / d\(x, y\).) Tj
T*
(   det\(B\) = d\(x, y\) / d\(r, theta\).) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore:) Tj
T*
(   d\(u, v\) / d\(r, theta\) = [ d\(u, v\) / d\(x, y\) ] * [ d\(x, y\) / d\(r, theta\) ].) Tj
T*
(   Hence proved.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
