(   [Problem Statement]: Verify that the functions u = \(x - y\) / \(x + y\) and v = \(x * y\) / \(x + y\)^2 are functionally dependent. Find the explicit functional relation connecting u and v.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Compute partial derivatives of u = \(x - y\) / \(x + y\):) Tj
T*
(   du/dx = [ \(x + y\)*1 - \(x - y\)*1 ] / \(x + y\)^2 = 2y / \(x + y\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   du/dy = [ \(x + y\)*\(-1\) - \(x - y\)*1 ] / \(x + y\)^2 = -2x / \(x + y\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Compute partial derivatives of v = \(x * y\) / \(x + y\)^2:) Tj
T*
(   dv/dx = [ \(x + y\)^2 * y - xy * 2\(x + y\) ] / \(x + y\)^4) Tj
T*
(   = [ y*\(x + y\) - 2xy ] / \(x + y\)^3 = \(xy + y^2 - 2xy\) / \(x + y\)^3) Tj
T*
(   = y*\(y - x\) / \(x + y\)^3.) Tj
T*
(   dv/dy = [ \(x + y\)^2 * x - xy * 2\(x + y\) ] / \(x + y\)^4) Tj
T*
(   = [ x*\(x + y\) - 2xy ] / \(x + y\)^3 = \(x^2 + xy - 2xy\) / \(x + y\)^3) Tj
T*
(   = x*\(x - y\) / \(x + y\)^3.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Evaluate the Jacobian determinant J = d\(u, v\) / d\(x, y\):) Tj
T*
(   J = \(du/dx\)*\(dv/dy\) - \(du/dy\)*\(dv/dx\)) Tj
T*
(   = [ 2y / \(x + y\)^2 ] * [ x*\(x - y\) / \(x + y\)^3 ] - [ -2x / \(x + y\)^2 ] * [ y*\(y - x\) / \(x +) Tj
T*
(   y\)^3 ]) Tj
T*
(   = [ 2xy*\(x - y\) / \(x + y\)^5 ] + [ 2xy*\(y - x\) / \(x + y\)^5 ]) Tj
T*
(   = [ 2xy*\(x - y\) - 2xy*\(x - y\) ] / \(x + y\)^5 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Since J = 0 identically, the functions u and v are strictly FUNCTIONALLY DEPENDENT.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Find the Functional Relation:) Tj
T*
(   Consider u^2:) Tj
T*
(   u^2 = \(x - y\)^2 / \(x + y\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   Expand the numerator:) Tj
T*
(   \(x - y\)^2 = \(x + y\)^2 - 4xy.) Tj
T*
(   Substitute:) Tj
T*
(   u^2 = [ \(x + y\)^2 - 4xy ] / \(x + y\)^2 = 1 - 4 * [ xy / \(x + y\)^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   Recognize that v = xy / \(x + y\)^2:) Tj
T*
(   u^2 = 1 - 4 * v.) Tj
T*
(   Rearrange:) Tj
T*
(   u^2 + 4*v - 1 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The explicit functional relationship is: u^2 + 4v = 1 \(or v = \(1 - u^2\) / 4\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
