(>> Solution to Question 15:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: If x = u*\(1 - v\), y = u*v*\(1 - w\), and z = u*v*w, evaluate the Jacobian determinant: J = d\(x, y, z\) / d\(u, v, w\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Compute partial derivatives for row 1 \(derivatives of x = u - uv\):) Tj
T*
(   dx/du = 1 - v) Tj
T*
(   dx/dv = -u) Tj
T*
(   dx/dw = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Compute partial derivatives for row 2 \(derivatives of y = uv - uvw\):) Tj
T*
(   dy/du = v*\(1 - w\)) Tj
T*
(   dy/dv = u*\(1 - w\)) Tj
T*
(   dy/dw = -uv.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Compute partial derivatives for row 3 \(derivatives of z = uvw\):) Tj
T*
(   dz/du = vw) Tj
T*
(   dz/dv = uw) Tj
T*
ET

