(   [Problem Statement]: Expand f\(x, y\) = e^x * cos\(y\) in Maclaurin series about \(0, 0\) up to terms of degree 3.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Evaluate f and its partial derivatives at \(0, 0\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: f\(x, y\) = e^x * cos y => f\(0, 0\) = e^0 * cos 0 = 1.) Tj
T*
(   - First partial derivatives:) Tj
T*
(   fx = e^x * cos y => fx\(0, 0\) = 1.) Tj
T*
(   fy = -e^x * sin y => fy\(0, 0\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Second partial derivatives:) Tj
T*
(   fxx = e^x * cos y => fxx\(0, 0\) = 1.) Tj
T*
(   fxy = -e^x * sin y => fxy\(0, 0\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   fyy = -e^x * cos y => fyy\(0, 0\) = -1.) Tj
T*
(   - Third partial derivatives:) Tj
T*
(   fxxx = e^x * cos y => fxxx\(0, 0\) = 1.) Tj
T*
(   fxxy = -e^x * sin y => fxxy\(0, 0\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   fxyy = -e^x * cos y => fxyy\(0, 0\) = -1.) Tj
T*
(   fyyy = e^x * sin y => fyyy\(0, 0\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Assemble Taylor Series Terms about \(0, 0\):) Tj
T*
(   f\(x, y\) = f\(0, 0\) + [ x*fx + y*fy ] + \(1/2!\)*[ x^2*fxx + 2xy*fxy + y^2*fyy ]) Tj
T*
(   + \(1/3!\)*[ x^3*fxxx + 3x^2*y*fxxy + 3xy^2*fxyy + y^3*fyyy ] + ...) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Substitute values:) Tj
T*
(   - Constant term: 1.) Tj
T*
(   - First-degree terms: 1*x + 0*y = x.) Tj
T*
(   - Second-degree terms: \(1/2\)*[ 1*x^2 + 0 + \(-1\)*y^2 ] = \(1/2\)*\(x^2 - y^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Third-degree terms: \(1/6\)*[ 1*x^3 + 0 + 3xy^2*\(-1\) + 0 ] = \(1/6\)*\(x^3 - 3xy^2\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Combine:) Tj
T*
(   e^x * cos y = 1 + x + \(1/2\)*\(x^2 - y^2\) + \(1/6\)*\(x^3 - 3xy^2\) + ...) Tj
T*
(   Verification by Series Product:) Tj
T*
(   e^x = 1 + x + x^2/2 + x^3/6 + ...) Tj
T*
(   cos y = 1 - y^2/2 + ...) Tj
T*
(   Product = \(1 + x + x^2/2 + x^3/6\)*\(1 - y^2/2\) = 1 + x + x^2/2 - y^2/2 + x^3/6 - xy^2/2 + ...) Tj
T*
(   \(Matches exactly\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
