(   [Problem Statement]: State the necessary and sufficient conditions for local maxima, minima, and saddle points of a function of two variables f\(x, y\). Prove the discriminant criterion using the Hessian matrix.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Stationary \(Critical\) Points:) Tj
T*
(   - Necessary Condition: A point \(a, b\) is an extremum of a differentiable function f\(x, y\) only) Tj
T*
(   if its gradient vanishes:) Tj
T*
(   fx\(a, b\) = 0 and fy\(a, b\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   2. Second Derivative Test \(Discriminant Criterion\):) Tj
T*
(   - At stationary point \(a, b\), define second partial derivatives:) Tj
T*
(   r = fxx\(a, b\), s = fxy\(a, b\), t = fyy\(a, b\).) Tj
T*
(   - Discriminant: Delta = r * t - s^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Classification:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Delta > 0 and r < 0 \(or t < 0\): Local MAXIMUM at \(a, b\).) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Delta > 0 and r > 0 \(or t > 0\): Local MINIMUM at \(a, b\).) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) Delta < 0: SADDLE POINT at \(a, b\) \(neither max nor min\).) Tj
T*
(   \(d\) Delta = 0: Test is INCONCLUSIVE.) Tj
T*
(   3. Proof using Hessian Matrix and Taylor's Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   - Near stationary point \(a, b\), Taylor expansion with h = x - a, k = y - b:) Tj
T*
(   Delta_f = f\(a + h, b + k\) - f\(a, b\) = \(1/2\) * [ r * h^2 + 2s * h * k + t * k^2 ] + R_3.) Tj
T*
(   - The quadratic form is Q\(h, k\) = r * h^2 + 2s * hk + t * k^2 = [h, k] * H * [h; k],) Tj
T*
(   where H = [ r, s; s, t ] is the Hessian matrix.) Tj
T*
(   - Multiply and divide Q by r \(assuming r != 0\):) Tj
T*
(   Q\(h, k\) = \(1 / r\) * [ r^2 * h^2 + 2 * r * s * hk + r * t * k^2 ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(1 / r\) * [ \(r * h + s * k\)^2 + \(r * t - s^2\) * k^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Case 1: Delta = r*t - s^2 > 0:) Tj
T*
(   Then \(r*h + s*k\)^2 + Delta*k^2 is strictly positive for all \(h, k\) != \(0, 0\).) Tj
T*
(   The sign of Q\(h, k\) is determined solely by the scalar 1/r:) Tj
T*
(   * If r > 0: Q\(h, k\) > 0 for all small \(h, k\), so f\(x, y\) > f\(a, b\) => Local MINIMUM.) Tj
T*
(   * If r < 0: Q\(h, k\) < 0 for all small \(h, k\), so f\(x, y\) < f\(a, b\) => Local MAXIMUM.) Tj
T*
(   - Case 2: Delta = r*t - s^2 < 0:) Tj
T*
(   Along the line r*h + s*k = 0, Q = \(Delta / r\)*k^2 \(opposite sign of r\).) Tj
T*
(   Along k = 0, Q = r*h^2 \(same sign as r\).) Tj
T*
(   Thus Q assumes both positive and negative values in every neighborhood of \(a, b\).) Tj
T*
(   Hence, \(a, b\) is a SADDLE POINT. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
