(   [Problem Statement]: Find and classify all critical points of the function: f\(x, y\) = 4xy - x^4 - y^4.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: First Partial Derivatives:) Tj
T*
(   fx = 4y - 4x^3 = 4*\(y - x^3\)) Tj
T*
(   fy = 4x - 4y^3 = 4*\(x - y^3\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Stationary Points \(fx = 0 and fy = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   From fx = 0: y = x^3.) Tj
T*
(   Substitute into fy = 0:) Tj
T*
(   x - \(x^3\)^3 = 0 => x - x^9 = 0) Tj
T*
(   => x * \(1 - x^8\) = 0 => x * \(1 - x^4\)*\(1 + x^4\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   => x * \(1 - x^2\)*\(1 + x^2\)*\(1 + x^4\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   => x * \(1 - x\)*\(1 + x\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Real roots: x = 0, x = 1, x = -1.) Tj
T*
(   - If x = 0: y = 0^3 = 0. Point P1\(0, 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - If x = 1: y = 1^3 = 1. Point P2\(1, 1\).) Tj
T*
(   - If x = -1: y = \(-1\)^3 = -1. Point P3\(-1, -1\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Second Partial Derivatives:) Tj
T*
(   r = fxx = -12x^2) Tj
T*
