BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Find the maximum and minimum values of f\(x, y, z\) = x^2 + y^2 + z^2 subject to the constraint x + y + z = 3a \(a > 0\) using Lagrange's method.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Set up the Lagrange function:) Tj
T*
(   Objective function: f\(x, y, z\) = x^2 + y^2 + z^2.) Tj
T*
(   Constraint: phi\(x, y, z\) = x + y + z - 3a = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Auxiliary function:) Tj
T*
(   F\(x, y, z, lambda\) = x^2 + y^2 + z^2 + lambda * \(x + y + z - 3a\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Partial derivatives set to zero:) Tj
T*
(   dF/dx = 2x + lambda = 0 => x = -lambda / 2.) Tj
T*
(   dF/dy = 2y + lambda = 0 => y = -lambda / 2.) Tj
T*
(   dF/dz = 2z + lambda = 0 => z = -lambda / 2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Symmetry of variables:) Tj
T*
(   x = y = z = -lambda / 2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Substitute into the constraint:) Tj
T*
(   x + y + z = 3a) Tj
T*
(   => \(-lambda / 2\) + \(-lambda / 2\) + \(-lambda / 2\) = 3a) Tj
T*
(   => -3*lambda / 2 = 3a => lambda = -2a.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Compute coordinates:) Tj
T*
(   x = -\(-2a\) / 2 = a.) Tj
T*
(   y = a.) Tj
T*
(   z = a.) Tj
T*
(   Critical point: \(a, a, a\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 6: Determine Nature of Extremum:) Tj
T*
(   - Geometrically, f\(x, y, z\) represents the square of the distance from the origin to a point on) Tj
T*
(   the plane x + y + z = 3a.) Tj
T*
(   - As points on the plane recede to infinity, distance -> infinity.) Tj
T*
(   - Thus, the unique critical point \(a, a, a\) must be the global MINIMUM.) Tj
T*
(   - Minimum value:) Tj
T*
(   f_min = a^2 + a^2 + a^2 = 3*a^2.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The minimum value is 3*a^2 at \(a, a, a\). The function has no maximum \(unbounded above\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
