(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the equations of the tangent plane and normal line to a level surface F\(x, y, z\) = 0 at point P\(x0, y0, z0\). Find both equations for the ellipsoid 2*x^2 + 3*y^2 + z^2 = 21 at point \(1, 2, 3\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivations:) Tj
T*
(   - Let C: r\(t\) = [x\(t\), y\(t\), z\(t\)]^T be any curve lying on the surface F\(x, y, z\) = 0 passing) Tj
T*
(   through P\(x0, y0, z0\) at t = t0.) Tj
T*
(   - F\(x\(t\), y\(t\), z\(t\)\) = 0. Differentiating with respect to t:) Tj
T*
(   Fx * \(dx/dt\) + Fy * \(dy/dt\) + Fz * \(dz/dt\) = 0 => grad\(F\) . r'\(t0\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Since grad\(F\) is perpendicular to the tangent vector of every curve on the surface, grad\(F\)) Tj
T*
(   is NORMAL to the surface at P.) Tj
T*
(   - Tangent Plane Equation: Passes through P\(x0, y0, z0\) with normal vector [Fx, Fy, Fz]^T:) Tj
T*
(   Fx\(P\) * \(x - x0\) + Fy\(P\) * \(y - y0\) + Fz\(P\) * \(z - z0\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Normal Line Equation: Passes through P along direction [Fx, Fy, Fz]^T:) Tj
T*
(   \(x - x0\) / Fx\(P\) = \(y - y0\) / Fy\(P\) = \(z - z0\) / Fz\(P\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Computation for Ellipsoid F\(x, y, z\) = 2*x^2 + 3*y^2 + z^2 - 21 = 0 at P\(1, 2, 3\):) Tj
T*
(   - Compute partial derivatives at \(1, 2, 3\):) Tj
T*
(   Fx = 4x => Fx\(1, 2, 3\) = 4\(1\) = 4.) Tj
T*
(   Fy = 6y => Fy\(1, 2, 3\) = 6\(2\) = 12.) Tj
T*
(   Fz = 2z => Fz\(1, 2, 3\) = 2\(3\) = 6.) Tj
T*
(   - Tangent Plane:) Tj
T*
ET

