(>> Solution to Question 28:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: In biotechnology, optimize the dilution rate D and inlet substrate concentration S0 to maximize steady-state biomass productivity P\(D, S0\) = D * X in a chemostat, where biomass X = Y * [ S0 - \(Ks * D\) / \(mu_max - D\) ]. Formulate the optimization problem using multivariate calculus.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   - In a continuous chemostat bioprocess, steady-state biomass concentration is:) Tj
T*
(   X\(D, S0\) = Y * [ S0 - \(Ks * D\) / \(mu_max - D\) ],) Tj
T*
(   where Y is the biomass yield coefficient, Ks is the substrate saturation constant, and mu_max) Tj
T*
(   is maximum specific growth rate.) Tj
T*
(   - Volumetric biomass productivity is:) Tj
T*
(   P\(D, S0\) = D * X = Y * [ D * S0 - \(Ks * D^2\) / \(mu_max - D\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Objective: For a given substrate feed concentration S0, find optimal dilution rate D_opt that) Tj
T*
(   maximizes productivity P.) Tj
T*
(   2. Differentiate P with respect to D:) Tj
T*
(   dP / dD = Y * [ S0 - Ks * d/dD\( D^2 / \(mu_max - D\) \) ].) Tj
T*
(   Compute derivative of quotient:) Tj
T*
(   d/dD [ D^2 / \(mu_max - D\) ] = [ \(mu_max - D\)*\(2D\) - D^2*\(-1\) ] / \(mu_max - D\)^2) Tj
T*
(   = [ 2*mu_max*D - 2*D^2 + D^2 ] / \(mu_max - D\)^2) Tj
T*
(   = [ 2*mu_max*D - D^2 ] / \(mu_max - D\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   3. Set dP / dD = 0:) Tj
T*
(   S0 - Ks * [ \(2*mu_max*D - D^2\) / \(mu_max - D\)^2 ] = 0) Tj
T*
(   => Ks * \(2*mu_max*D - D^2\) = S0 * \(mu_max - D\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   Let alpha = S0 / Ks \(dimensionless substrate ratio\):) Tj
T*
(   2*mu_max*D - D^2 = alpha * \(mu_max^2 - 2*mu_max*D + D^2\)) Tj
T*
(   \(1 + alpha\) * D^2 - 2*\(1 + alpha\)*mu_max * D + alpha * mu_max^2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   4. Solve Quadratic Equation for D:) Tj
T*
(   Divide by \(1 + alpha\):) Tj
T*
(   D^2 - 2*mu_max * D + [ alpha / \(1 + alpha\) ] * mu_max^2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Using quadratic formula:) Tj
T*
(   D = mu_max +- sqrt\( mu_max^2 - [ alpha / \(1 + alpha\) ] * mu_max^2 \)) Tj
T*
(   = mu_max * [ 1 - sqrt\( 1 - alpha / \(1 + alpha\) \) ] \(reject + sign since D < mu_max\)) Tj
T*
(   = mu_max * [ 1 - sqrt\( 1 / \(1 + alpha\) \) ]) Tj
T*
(   = mu_max * [ 1 - sqrt\( Ks / \(Ks + S0\) \) ].) Tj
T*
(   5. Biochemical Significance:) Tj
T*
(   - When S0 >> Ks \(typical industrial operation, alpha >> 1\):) Tj
T*
(   sqrt\(Ks / \(Ks + S0\)\) ~ 0 => D_opt approaches mu_max.) Tj
T*
(   - The bioreactor operates near wash-out to achieve maximum biomass output per unit time.) Tj
T*
