/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A rectangular bioreactor cooling jacket has surface area S = 2*\(xy + yz + zx\) and fixed volume V = x*y*z = 1000 m^3. Use Lagrange's Method of Multipliers to find dimensions \(x, y, z\) that minimize heat loss surface area.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Formulate the Optimization Problem:) Tj
T*
(   Objective function \(Surface Area to minimize\):) Tj
T*
(   S\(x, y, z\) = 2*\(x*y + y*z + z*x\).) Tj
T*
(   Constraint \(Fixed Volume\):) Tj
T*
(   phi\(x, y, z\) = x*y*z - 1000 = 0 \(with x, y, z > 0\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Construct the Lagrange Auxiliary Function:) Tj
T*
(   F\(x, y, z, lambda\) = 2*\(xy + yz + zx\) + lambda * \(xyz - 1000\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Compute Partial Derivatives and Equate to Zero:) Tj
T*
(   dF/dx = 2*\(y + z\) + lambda * y*z = 0 => 2*\(y + z\) = -lambda * y*z. \(Eq. 1\)) Tj
T*
(   dF/dy = 2*\(x + z\) + lambda * x*z = 0 => 2*\(x + z\) = -lambda * x*z. \(Eq. 2\)) Tj
T*
(   dF/dz = 2*\(x + y\) + lambda * x*y = 0 => 2*\(x + y\) = -lambda * x*y. \(Eq. 3\)) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Divide Eq. 1 by y*z, Eq. 2 by x*z, Eq. 3 by x*y:) Tj
T*
(   From Eq. 1: 2*\(1/z + 1/y\) = -lambda.) Tj
T*
(   From Eq. 2: 2*\(1/z + 1/x\) = -lambda.) Tj
T*
(   From Eq. 3: 2*\(1/y + 1/x\) = -lambda.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Equate pairs:) Tj
T*
