(   2*\(1/z + 1/y\) = 2*\(1/z + 1/x\) => 1/y = 1/x => x = y.) Tj
T*
(   2*\(1/z + 1/x\) = 2*\(1/y + 1/x\) => 1/z = 1/y => y = z.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore, by symmetry:) Tj
T*
(   x = y = z \(a perfect cube!\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 6: Solve for dimensions using the constraint:) Tj
T*
(   x * y * z = 1000) Tj
T*
(   => x^3 = 1000 => x = \(1000\)^\(1/3\) = 10 m.) Tj
T*
(   Thus:) Tj
T*
(   x = 10 m, y = 10 m, z = 10 m.) Tj
T*
(   Step 7: Minimum Surface Area:) Tj
T*
(   S_min = 2 * [ 10\(10\) + 10\(10\) + 10\(10\) ] = 2 * [ 100 + 100 + 100 ] = 2 * 300 = 600 m^2.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The heat loss surface area is minimized when the bioreactor jacket is a cube with dimensions 10) Tj
T*
(   m x 10 m x 10 m, yielding a minimum surface area of 600 m^2.) Tj
